1. Introduction

This document provides the implementation blueprint for the Orbital Star Ring Smart City’s QUENNE Stack. It translates the architectural specifications (QS-OSR-ARCH-001) into concrete development, integration, deployment, and operational practices. It is intended for engineering teams responsible for building, testing, and sustaining the system.

The implementation follows DevSecOps principles adapted for long‑life, high‑reliability space systems. All artifacts – source code, configuration, simulation models, test harnesses – are managed in a single digital engineering ecosystem.

---

2. Implementation Principles

Principle Application
Code First, Model Aware SysML models are kept in sync with code via model‑to‑text transformations. Every interface change starts in the model.
Test as You Fly The final orbital hardware runs the same binary that passed acceptance on ground. Simulation substitutes only sensors/actuators.
Formal Methods for Critical Paths seL4, SPARK, and TLA⁺ are mandatory for TMR‑voted components (Triad, QNI, attitude control).
Infrastructure as Code All network, container, and configuration definitions are versioned and reviewed.
Immutable Artifacts Every build produces a cryptographically signed bundle (OS image, container, FPGA bitstream) that is traceable to source.
Progressive Deployment Capabilities are added in small, reversible increments; rollback is always possible.

