4.2 Layer 2 – Linux Core Algorithm

Purpose: Provide a real‑time, secure, open‑source operating environment.

Implementation:

· Kernel: Linux 6.6 LTS with PREEMPT_RT patch set, configured for minimal footprint.
· Space Hardening: EDAC (Error Detection And Correction) drivers enabled; soft‑error recovery via periodic cache scrubbing.
· Init System: systemd with critical services marked Before=local-fs.target.
· Root Filesystem: SquashFS, read‑only, with overlay for runtime state.
· Build System: Yocto Kirkstone, custom meta‑starring layer.

Yocto Recipe Snippet (recipes-kernel/linux/linux-starring_6.6.bb):

```bitbake
SRC_URI = "git://kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/stable/linux.git;branch=linux-6.6.y \
           file://preempt_rt.cfg \
           file://starring_defconfig \
           file://edac.cfg"
KERNEL_VERSION = "6.6.21-rt22"
```

Container Runtime: containerd + runsc (gVisor) for strong isolation between non‑trusted workloads (e.g., resident apps).
Over‑the‑Air Updates: OSTree + Aktualizr; updates are signed and can be atomically rolled back.

