6. Deployment Orchestration

6.1 Ground Development & Test

· Kubernetes on x86 clusters simulates the distributed nature of the ring.
· Each QUENNE layer runs in a separate namespace; inter‑layer communication is via Kubernetes Services.
· Helm charts parameterise simulation vs. hardware deployments.

6.2 Orbital Deployment

No full Kubernetes in orbit (overhead too high). Instead, a lightweight orchestrator is custom‑built:

· Node Agent: Written in Rust, runs on every compute node.
· Desired State Store: etcd cluster (5 nodes) replicated across segments.
· Deployment Units: OCI‑compatible containers (for application layers) and Yocto images (for base OS).
· Rollout Controller: Ensures gradual, canary‑style updates; automatic rollback on health check failure.

Deployment Manifest Example (YAML):

```yaml
apiVersion: starring.quenne/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: sensor-fusion
spec:
  replicas: 8
  selector:
    nodeType: fusion
  container:
    image: starring/sensor-fusion:2.1.0
    resources:
      gpu: 1
      memory: 32Gi
  health:
    grpcProbe: /health
  updatePolicy:
    maxUnavailable: 1
    canaryDuration: 300s
```

