8. Security Implementation

8.1 Identity and Access Management

· SPIFFE SPIFFE IDs are assigned to every workload (e.g., spiffe://starring/ns/layer7/sa/fusion).
· SPIRE server runs on the Triad nodes, issues SVIDs (X.509 certificates) with short validity.
· mTLS enforced for all gRPC and DDS communications.

8.2 Secrets Management

· HashiCorp Vault (space‑rated) stores keys, passwords, and certificates.
· Secrets are injected via Vault Agent sidecars or Kubernetes Secrets (encrypted at rest).

8.3 Network Segmentation

· VLANs separate trust zones; TTEthernet Virtual Links are statically configured.
· Wireless networks use WPA3‑Enterprise with per‑device certificates.

8.4 Audit and Compliance

· All security‑relevant events are logged to the blockchain.
· Regular automated compliance scans (OpenSCAP) on all Linux nodes.

