9. Fault Tolerance and Resilience Implementation

9.1 Triple Modular Redundancy (TMR)

· Implemented at hardware level for Triad, reactor controllers, and attitude sensors.
· For software TMR, three independently developed implementations (e.g., C, Ada, Rust) vote on outputs.

9.2 Byzantine Fault Tolerance

· The etcd cluster uses Raft with 5 nodes; handles crash faults.
· For state machine replication that must tolerate Byzantine faults (e.g., ethical audit log), Hyperledger Fabric with PBFT is used.

9.3 Graceful Degradation

· Each component publishes a health status and capability level (0–100%).
· The Booster Scheduler reallocates tasks based on available capabilities.
· Example: if 30% of photonic cores fail, attitude control falls back to electronic PID, albeit with higher jitter.

9.4 Chaos Engineering Implementation

· Chaos Mesh (ground) and a custom fault injector (orbit) periodically kill processes, partition networks, corrupt memory.
· Post‑mortems are automated using Jupyter notebooks analysing traces and logs.

