10.1 Continuous Verification Pipeline

```
[Commit] → [Model Consistency Check] → [Static Analysis] → [Unit Tests] → [Integration Tests] → [HITL] → [Acceptance]
```

10.2 Formal Verification of Critical Components

· seL4 kernel: Proof of correctness already exists; we verify configuration and initialisation.
· QNI plasma control: SPARK Ada code proven free of runtime errors; invariant proofs for density limits.
· Ethical rules: TLA⁺ model of the reasoner; model checking ensures no rule contradiction.

10.3 Hardware‑in‑the‑Loop (HITL)

· A full‑scale electrical testbed (without radiation) replicates the compute nodes and networks.
· Real reactor sensors are stimulated with simulated plasma signals.
· Photonic chip is exercised with optical inputs from laser diodes.

10.4 Orbital Validation

· The ISS Star Ring Node runs the full QUENNE stack in a representative environment for 6 months.
· Performance, reliability, and correctness metrics are collected and compared to ground predictions.

